# Architecture

## Runtime

- Vite + React + strict TypeScript.
- One root `CakeProvider` in `src/App.tsx`.
- `styled-components` for prototype-specific composition.
- Cake& CSS custom properties for every visual value.
- `lucide-react` or exact exported Figma assets for icons.
- Tauri frameless shell (`src-tauri/`) for local Windows-app launch via
  `npm run start:windows`, rendering through the OS webview.
- Electron frameless shell (`electron/`) kept as a Rust-free alternative via
  `npm run start:electron`.
- `src/desktop/windowApi.ts` presents one caption-control contract to the UI and
  resolves it to the Tauri window API or the Electron `window.vantageDesktop`
  preload bridge at runtime.

## Structure

- `src/components/shell/`: Windows frame, title bar, sidebar, and command bar.
- `src/components/dashboard/`: Home dashboard cards and status visuals.
- `src/components/prototype/`: non-production scenario controls.
- `src/data/`: typed mock data, thresholds, and state fixtures.
- `src/assets/`: exact downloaded Figma assets.
- `src/styles/`: token-only layout and global prototype composition.
- `src/desktop/`: typed bridge to the host window APIs.
- `src-tauri/`: Tauri Rust shell, window config, and capability permissions.
- `electron/`: Electron main process, preload bridge, and local launch script.
- `src/test/`: test setup and accessibility helpers.

## State flow

`App` owns the selected destination, scenario, carousel pages, and transient
feedback. It passes typed data and callbacks into presentational shell and
dashboard components. No backend or persistence is introduced in Phase 1.

## Design-system gaps

Figma-specific radial status gauges, pager dots, Windows caption controls, and
the OS Mica shell recipe may be composed locally only when Cake& has no exported
equivalent. Each local composition must use Cake& tokens and be documented.
